# ---- merge queue: a row GitHub keeps answering 404 for (BH-784) ---------------
# Since the queue reads its rows over REST, a 404 is a fact ("this PR is gone")
# and a 403/5xx is not ("I could not tell") — bin/merge-queue.sh keeps them
# apart and NEVER dequeues on either. A 404 therefore leaves the row queued, and
# without a count it would sit there silently forever. This is how many
# CONSECUTIVE 404 reads on one row before exactly one ALERTS.log line names the
# project, the PR number and the row path. Any readable tick clears the counter,
# so a row only reaches this number while GitHub genuinely keeps saying 404.
# The counter starts at 1, so 0 means the alert never fires.
#MQ_ABSENT_ALERT_AFTER=3
